; Project-level registry pin: always resolve against the public npm registry,
; regardless of any machine-level registry override in ~/.npmrc.
;
; This is not a precaution — it is a repair. A developer ~/.npmrc on the
; release machine pointed at a local verdaccio mirror
; (http://localhost:4873/). Without this pin, npm commands run from this
; directory went to the mirror and reported success there: `npm dist-tag add`
; moved the tag on verdaccio while the public registry was left untouched
; (measured 2026-08-06). Nothing failed, nothing warned — the mistake read as
; a completed release. Keep this file even when it looks redundant.
registry=https://registry.npmjs.org/
